A||||8||Gokart||Moving battery up front.||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||04-27-2000||06:29 AM||||Who's got the best kit for this project? I've heard complaints about V8 Archies kit and Chris West's looks steel on his web site. Does anyone make a non-metal battery box?||||reg||5
Z||000001||lennyb4||04-27-2000||09:23 AM||||Yes. I just bought a kit from Summit Auto in Ohio and i really like it. it comes w/everything needed to move the battery. Cables, Box, Bolts, etc.. You can find them at <A HREF="http://WWW.SummitAutoRacing.com" TARGET=_blank>WWW.SummitAutoRacing.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||jhogans||04-27-2000||10:06 AM||||Lenny,<P>That link did not work.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lennyb4||04-27-2000||10:10 AM||||Oppss....sorry guys the actual link should be <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||04-27-2000||10:34 AM||||Chris West's box is actually made of aluminum and in my opinion, a little over priced, but well made (I have one). There are dangers in using a metal box, you sure don't want the terminals to make contact.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Frank R||04-27-2000||10:57 AM||||Plastic battery boxes come in a variety of sizes.  They are readily available at most boat shops.  They come with a top or box cover. These boxes prevent any battery gases or vapor from destroying nearby metal. You can make cable holes where ever needed.  Battery cables are available at any welding supply store in a great range of sizes.  Some large welding companys have used cable, that can be purchased very reasonably.  In relocating battery, always use 2 seperate conductors for the cables and attach very securely every few feet under car.  The source of the cable will have the tools parts and knowledge to attach large swaged or crimped terminal ends.  Frank R.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Gokart||04-30-2000||06:24 AM||||Found a boat shop on my route that has everything I need. Plastic box w/cover, cable, hardware,etc. Going to pick up tomorrow, what gauge wire am I getting for this project and will 6 feet be enough?||||reg||14
Z||000007||batboy||04-30-2000||08:42 AM||||I'm using 2 gauge with my setup, you could use 4 gauge though. Since my car has a V8, I decided to go with overkill. Six foot long cables might be a little short, mine were about 8 foot long (I think). I started out with 10 feet and trimmed a foot or two off. Most high end stereo stores have battery terminators (got mine at Crutchfields. I bought my 2 gauge welding wire in bulk at a Farm and Ranch store. They even has 0 and 00 gauge wire as well as 4, 6, and 8 gauge. I'm not sure how you're going to install that universal box and still have a spare without cutting the spare tire well and fabricating a way to mount it. I'm sure it can be done, just might not be real easy. Maybe you can email Phil and ask him to snail mail you a copy of my instructions for my battery box I installed. Also, I posted a topic and pics of my mod a while back too.||||reg||1
Z||000008||JIM GOOSE||04-30-2000||09:01 AM||||I did this conversion several years ago and you can see more details at <A HREF="http://www.hamptonmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.hamptonmotorsports.com</A> ||||reg||3
